course: dictionary
lesson: 4225
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Grain» is a good example. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» Rice, wheat and maize are plants we eat, so grain here means the seeds of plants used for food. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: «A microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin.» The words size and rice tell you that grain means one tiny hard piece, like a single grain of rice. Context clues point to the right meaning.
explain: Some words sit in phrases that have their own meaning. «A grain of truth» means a very small amount of truth, not a piece of food. When a word seems odd, read the whole phrase and ask what the writer is trying to say.
fact: Grain is the seeds of plants like wheat, rice, oats, barley and corn, used for food.
fact: A grain is one tiny hard piece of something, like a grain of sand, salt or sugar.
fact: «A grain of truth» means a very small amount of truth.
fact: Whole grains, such as brown rice, oats and wholemeal bread, are good food.
fact: Flour is ground grain.
exercise: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» What does grain mean in this sentence? | A very small amount of anything | The pattern of lines in wood | One tiny hard piece of sand | *Seeds of plants used for food
exercise: «House mice mainly eat seeds, grain and crumbs.» What kind of thing is grain here? | A kind of cheese | *Seeds from plants, used as food | Lines in a piece of wood | A tiny piece of sand
exercise: Mia says grain in «a grain of truth» means a food. What does it really mean? | *A tiny amount of truth | A kind of rice | A piece of wood | A bowl of oats
test: Dad says the grain of the table runs along its length. What does grain mean? | *The pattern of lines in wood | A tiny hard piece of salt | A little bit of luck | The seeds of wheat
test: Which of these is a whole grain? | Sugar | Sand | Cheese | *Brown rice
exam: «A grain of sand fell into my shoe.» In this sentence, what does grain mean? | The pattern of lines in wood | A rule that nobody follows | The seeds of plants used for food | *One tiny hard piece of something
